1
00:00:02,960 --> 00:00:05,710
Guys! Guys! I've got great news. Guess what.

2
00:00:06,420 --> 00:00:08,250
Uh, Monica's pregnant!

3
00:00:06,420 --> 00:00:08,250
Really?

4
00:00:10,720 --> 00:00:12,800
Let's get past the moment.

5
00:00:13,180 --> 00:00:14,840
What's your news?

6
00:00:13,180 --> 00:00:14,840
Thank you.

7
00:00:15,260 --> 00:00:17,260
I got a job in advertising.

8
00:00:18,640 --> 00:00:20,470
Oh, honey, that's incredible!

9
00:00:18,640 --> 00:00:20,470
Wow.

10
00:00:20,680 --> 00:00:23,440
Gosh, what's the pay like?

11
00:00:25,440 --> 00:00:27,730
Oh, come on, people.

12
00:00:27,900 --> 00:00:29,900
If I don't know who makes the most...

13
00:00:30,070 --> 00:00:32,610
how do I know who I like the most? Hi, Joey.

14
00:00:35,160 --> 00:00:37,120
It pays nothing. It's an internship.

15
00:00:37,320 --> 00:00:39,200
We have interns at Days of our Lives.

16
00:00:39,410 --> 00:00:42,460
Right. So it'll be the same, except less sex with you.

17
00:00:44,420 --> 00:00:46,580
So, uh, what do you think they'll have you do there?

18
00:00:46,750 --> 00:00:49,920
It's a training program, but they hire the people they like.

19
00:00:50,090 --> 00:00:53,090
That's great!

20
00:00:50,090 --> 00:00:53,090
There's gonna be some grunt work...

21
00:00:53,260 --> 00:00:56,890
which will stink. A grown man getting people coffee is humiliating.

22
00:00:59,760 --> 00:01:02,350
Humiliating and noble.

23
00:01:03,310 --> 00:01:05,230
Thank you.

24
00:01:06,900 --> 00:01:09,070
You know, if I didn't already have a job...

25
00:01:09,230 --> 00:01:11,320
I would've been good in advertising.

26
00:01:11,480 --> 00:01:14,240
Ross, you did not come up with "got milk?"

27
00:01:14,400 --> 00:01:16,410
Yes, I did! I did!

28
00:01:18,410 --> 00:01:21,120
I should've written it down.

29
00:02:12,340 --> 00:02:13,380
Hey.

30
00:02:12,340 --> 00:02:13,380
Hey.

31
00:02:13,550 --> 00:02:16,800
Where's Chandler? I wanna wish him good luck on his first day.

32
00:02:17,010 --> 00:02:19,470
And I smelled bacon. Ha, ha.

33
00:02:20,140 --> 00:02:22,890
He just left.

34
00:02:20,140 --> 00:02:22,890
Who did?

35
00:02:24,720 --> 00:02:27,180
Joey, you're never gonna believe it! She called!

36
00:02:27,930 --> 00:02:29,100
She did'?

37
00:02:27,930 --> 00:02:29,100
You got it!

38
00:02:29,100 --> 00:02:30,770
I did?

39
00:02:29,100 --> 00:02:30,770
What is she talking about?

40
00:02:30,980 --> 00:02:33,190
I don't know, but it sounds great!

41
00:02:33,360 --> 00:02:35,530
No, your agent called. You got that audition!

42
00:02:35,730 --> 00:02:37,070
With Leonard Hayes?

43
00:02:35,730 --> 00:02:37,070
Yes!

44
00:02:37,240 --> 00:02:40,950
Oh, my God, that is great! It's for a play on Broadway.

45
00:02:41,120 --> 00:02:45,240
And in a real theater. Not that little one underneath the deli like last time.

46
00:02:45,450 --> 00:02:47,080
Is it a good play'?

47
00:02:45,450 --> 00:02:47,080
It must be.

48
00:02:48,410 --> 00:02:50,870
I read it and didn't understand a single word!

49
00:02:51,040 --> 00:02:53,750
Leonard Hayes is starring in it.

50
00:02:51,040 --> 00:02:53,750
Yeah, and directing.

51
00:02:53,920 --> 00:02:56,420
Oh, he was so good in that movie of Macbeth.

52
00:02:56,630 --> 00:03:00,430
You saw that?

53
00:02:56,630 --> 00:03:00,430
No, but I saw the previews.

54
00:03:00,590 --> 00:03:02,640
They played it right before Jackass.

55
00:03:00,590 --> 00:03:02,640
Ah.

56
00:03:02,800 --> 00:03:04,260
Oh, yeah, yeah. He has.

57
00:03:04,430 --> 00:03:06,390
He's done some amazing work.

58
00:03:04,430 --> 00:03:06,390
Oh, yeah.

59
00:03:06,560 --> 00:03:08,730
Oh, I loved him in those phone commercials.

60
00:03:08,890 --> 00:03:12,770
When the monkey hits him in the face with the giant rubber phone. Ha-ha-ha.

61
00:03:12,940 --> 00:03:14,900
Maybe the monkey will be at the audition.

62
00:03:15,110 --> 00:03:17,400
Don't make me more nervous than I already am!

63
00:03:27,830 --> 00:03:30,580
Good morning.

64
00:03:27,830 --> 00:03:30,580
Can I get you a cup of coffee, sir?

65
00:03:30,750 --> 00:03:33,710
Oh, no, no. I'm an intern, just like you guys.

66
00:03:33,880 --> 00:03:38,460
Except for the tie, the briefcase and the fact that I can rent a car.

67
00:03:38,670 --> 00:03:40,470
Seriously, you're an intern?

68
00:03:40,630 --> 00:03:44,180
I'm heading in a new career direction and you gotta start at the bottom.

69
00:03:44,930 --> 00:03:46,640
Dude.

70
00:03:47,850 --> 00:03:53,060
I know I'm a little older than you guys, but it's not like I'm Bob Hope.

71
00:03:55,980 --> 00:03:58,110
The comedian. USO.

72
00:03:59,740 --> 00:04:01,610
Uh, it's U.S.A., sir.

73
00:04:09,120 --> 00:04:12,160
This is Joey Tribbiani. Joey, these are the producers.

74
00:04:12,330 --> 00:04:15,290
And as you probably already know, this is Leonard Hayes.

75
00:04:15,920 --> 00:04:17,750
Wow.

76
00:04:19,420 --> 00:04:23,840
It is so amazing to meet you. I am such a big fan of your work.

77
00:04:24,680 --> 00:04:27,510
Well, I've been blessed with a lot of great roles.

78
00:04:27,680 --> 00:04:32,850
Tell me about it, huh? "Unlimited nights and weekends!"

79
00:04:34,020 --> 00:04:37,310
Are you making fun of me? Because I am not a sellout.

80
00:04:37,520 --> 00:04:40,190
I didn't do it for money. I believe in those phones!

81
00:04:40,360 --> 00:04:44,740
I almost lost a cousin because of bad wireless service.

82
00:04:44,950 --> 00:04:49,080
No, I wasn't making fun of you. I think you were great in those commercials.

83
00:04:49,240 --> 00:04:50,580
Really?

84
00:04:49,240 --> 00:04:50,580
Yeah.

85
00:04:50,740 --> 00:04:53,830
Well, I do bring a certain credibility to the role.

86
00:04:54,040 --> 00:04:55,460
It's true.

87
00:04:54,040 --> 00:04:55,460
Are you kidding?

88
00:04:55,620 --> 00:04:57,250
When they shoot you out of that cannon...

89
00:04:59,130 --> 00:05:01,300
"Hang up that phone!"

90
00:05:01,880 --> 00:05:03,170
One take.

91
00:05:01,880 --> 00:05:03,170
Wow.

92
00:05:03,380 --> 00:05:05,050
Did that in one. I know.

93
00:05:05,220 --> 00:05:08,260
So shall we read?

94
00:05:05,220 --> 00:05:08,260
Oh, yeah, sure.

95
00:05:08,430 --> 00:05:11,810
Top of Act 2. This is my entrance. You got it?

96
00:05:11,970 --> 00:05:13,770
Mm-hm.

97
00:05:16,020 --> 00:05:18,650
What the hell are you still doing here?

98
00:05:19,320 --> 00:05:21,070
Oh. Uh.

99
00:05:21,230 --> 00:05:23,610
I think you know.

100
00:05:21,230 --> 00:05:23,610
Bastard!

101
00:05:23,820 --> 00:05:27,320
I am what you made me. You know what? I could go right now.

102
00:05:27,530 --> 00:05:30,200
Go! Go!

103
00:05:27,530 --> 00:05:30,200
I can't.

104
00:05:30,370 --> 00:05:34,080
Oh, I want to, Long Pause...

105
00:05:36,250 --> 00:05:38,380
but I can't.

106
00:05:39,250 --> 00:05:45,300
I'm so sorry. You're not supposed to say "long pause."

107
00:05:46,930 --> 00:05:51,310
Oh! Oh, I thought that was your character's name. You know?

108
00:05:51,470 --> 00:05:54,930
I thought you were, like, an Indian or something, you know, with the...

109
00:05:55,100 --> 00:05:56,850
Sorry.

110
00:05:55,100 --> 00:05:56,850
Long Pause.

111
00:05:57,020 --> 00:06:00,900
No. Thank you so much for coming in. We appreciate it. Thank you.

112
00:06:01,070 --> 00:06:02,900
Sure you don't want me to do it again?

113
00:06:03,070 --> 00:06:04,690
I could do it with an accent.

114
00:06:03,070 --> 00:06:04,690
No.

115
00:06:04,860 --> 00:06:06,030
You know, Southern.

116
00:06:06,200 --> 00:06:08,610
"I could go right now, mon!"

117
00:06:08,780 --> 00:06:09,950
Huh?

118
00:06:12,530 --> 00:06:14,700
My God in heaven.

119
00:06:15,250 --> 00:06:20,170
Joey, hang on for a second. Leonard, can we talk to you for a moment?

120
00:06:20,330 --> 00:06:21,380
Yes?

121
00:06:23,090 --> 00:06:25,090
You've gotta be kidding. See, he can't act.

122
00:06:26,880 --> 00:06:28,510
I don't care if you think he's hot.

123
00:06:28,680 --> 00:06:31,720
If you wanna sleep with him, do it on your own time. This is a play.

124
00:06:33,890 --> 00:06:35,720
No, listen, if you insist on this...

125
00:06:35,890 --> 00:06:37,940
I will call my agent so fast...

126
00:06:38,100 --> 00:06:42,110
on a cell phone connection so clear, he's gonna think I'm next door!

127
00:06:43,980 --> 00:06:48,520
Uh, hi. Uh, thank you so much for whispering for my benefit.

128
00:06:48,740 --> 00:06:52,990
If you tell me what I did wrong, I would love to work on it and try it again for you.

129
00:06:53,160 --> 00:06:55,490
And also, how you doing?

130
00:06:58,830 --> 00:07:02,960
Would you please just give me another chance? I really wanna get better. Please?

131
00:07:03,130 --> 00:07:04,170
Really?

132
00:07:05,050 --> 00:07:07,260
Well, if you wanna come back today...

133
00:07:07,260 --> 00:07:09,170
here are my notes. Ready?

134
00:07:07,260 --> 00:07:09,170
Yeah.

135
00:07:09,380 --> 00:07:12,140
Um, you're in your head. You're thinking way too much.

136
00:07:12,340 --> 00:07:14,560
I really doubt that.

137
00:07:15,140 --> 00:07:19,020
No, no, no. It's that you're not connected with anything in your body.

138
00:07:19,230 --> 00:07:21,480
No urgency. The scene is a struggle.

139
00:07:19,230 --> 00:07:21,480
Uh-huh.

140
00:07:21,650 --> 00:07:22,730
It's a race.

141
00:07:21,650 --> 00:07:22,730
Uh-huh.

142
00:07:22,900 --> 00:07:25,150
Also, what you did was horizontal.

143
00:07:25,320 --> 00:07:28,990
Don't be afraid to explore the vertical.

144
00:07:25,320 --> 00:07:28,990
Uh-huh.

145
00:07:29,150 --> 00:07:33,700
And don't learn the words. Let the words learn you.

146
00:07:38,620 --> 00:07:40,580
Couldn't I just sleep with the producer?

147
00:07:44,710 --> 00:07:46,800
Hey, do you wanna go to dinner tonight?

148
00:07:46,960 --> 00:07:50,550
Oh, I can't. I've got a date with that waitress, Katie.

149
00:07:50,720 --> 00:07:54,140
Yeah, I know we've only gone out, like, twice, but I don't know...

150
00:07:54,300 --> 00:07:58,930
I have a good feeling about her.

151
00:07:54,300 --> 00:07:58,930
Oh, I hear divorce bells.

152
00:07:59,310 --> 00:08:01,980
Give me your wallets, and there won't be a problem.

153
00:08:02,140 --> 00:08:03,940
What?

154
00:08:02,140 --> 00:08:03,940
I have a gun.

155
00:08:04,150 --> 00:08:07,320
Okay, just relax, Phoebe. Just stay calm.

156
00:08:09,280 --> 00:08:11,740
Oh, my God, I can't find my wallet!

157
00:08:13,700 --> 00:08:17,410
All right, lady, now give me your purse.

158
00:08:13,700 --> 00:08:17,410
No.

159
00:08:17,620 --> 00:08:21,160
What do you mean, "no"? I knew you'd be my death, Phoebe Buffay!

160
00:08:22,580 --> 00:08:25,420
Lowell, is that you?

161
00:08:22,580 --> 00:08:25,420
Phoebe?

162
00:08:25,630 --> 00:08:30,300
Oh, my God!

163
00:08:25,630 --> 00:08:30,300
Unbelievable! Oh, my God! Oh!

164
00:08:30,460 --> 00:08:34,930
I'm sorry. Ross, this is my old friend, Lowell, from the streets! Ha, ha.

165
00:08:35,090 --> 00:08:37,510
Lowell, Ross.

166
00:08:35,090 --> 00:08:37,510
Ross, nice to meet you.

167
00:08:37,720 --> 00:08:39,850
Yeah, a real pleasure.

168
00:08:40,770 --> 00:08:44,430
Oh, it's been so long! Oh, so long.

169
00:08:40,770 --> 00:08:44,430
Ha-ha-ha.

170
00:08:44,480 --> 00:08:47,940
I can't believe you're still doing this.

171
00:08:44,480 --> 00:08:47,940
Ah, I know. But I quit smoking.

172
00:08:48,150 --> 00:08:49,900
Good for you.

173
00:08:50,070 --> 00:08:51,780
You look like you're doing well.

174
00:08:51,990 --> 00:08:53,360
I guess your mugging days are behind you.

175
00:08:53,570 --> 00:08:54,610
Oh.

176
00:08:54,780 --> 00:08:58,120
Oh, my God. Phoebe, you used to mug people?

177
00:08:59,620 --> 00:09:02,540
Excuse me, Ross, old friends catching up.

178
00:09:06,630 --> 00:09:07,790
HeY!

179
00:09:06,630 --> 00:09:07,790
HeY!

180
00:09:07,960 --> 00:09:11,420
How'd the audition go?

181
00:09:07,960 --> 00:09:11,420
They wanna see me again, but, uh...

182
00:09:11,590 --> 00:09:14,340
boy, Leonard Hayes did not like me.

183
00:09:14,510 --> 00:09:18,180
What happened?

184
00:09:14,510 --> 00:09:18,180
Oh, he said I wasn't urgent enough.

185
00:09:18,350 --> 00:09:23,680
Everything I did was horizontal, and I should be more vertical.

186
00:09:24,430 --> 00:09:28,110
Oh, and he said that I should think less.

187
00:09:24,430 --> 00:09:28,110
Well, so far so good.

188
00:09:30,190 --> 00:09:32,280
Honey, I'm old!

189
00:09:34,070 --> 00:09:34,860
What's wrong?

190
00:09:34,860 --> 00:09:39,990
I am so much older than these other interns. I can't compete with them.

191
00:09:40,160 --> 00:09:41,700
So you're a little older.

192
00:09:41,870 --> 00:09:44,830
Look at the positive. You have all this life experience.

193
00:09:45,040 --> 00:09:50,590
Yes, but I don't think life experience is gonna help me with these.

194
00:09:50,840 --> 00:09:56,220
Wow! It's like they're on fire!

195
00:09:56,380 --> 00:09:58,180
Ooh.

196
00:10:01,180 --> 00:10:03,430
What are they?

197
00:10:01,180 --> 00:10:03,430
Prototype sneakers.

198
00:10:04,180 --> 00:10:06,670
I need ideas on how to sell them. Which I can't do...

199
00:10:06,850 --> 00:10:09,310
because no self-respecting adult would ever wear these.

200
00:10:09,310 --> 00:10:10,860
I'll give you $500 for them.

201
00:10:15,030 --> 00:10:18,070
What am I supposed to do?

202
00:10:15,030 --> 00:10:18,070
Come on, sneakers are easy.

203
00:10:18,240 --> 00:10:21,950
You wear them all the time.

204
00:10:18,240 --> 00:10:21,950
They're not called sneakers anymore.

205
00:10:22,120 --> 00:10:28,040
They're called "kicks" or "skids." I think I heard somebody say "slorps."

206
00:10:29,580 --> 00:10:33,340
They've got wheels that pop out from the bottom so you can roll around...

207
00:10:33,500 --> 00:10:36,920
because apparently walking is too much exercise.

208
00:10:37,090 --> 00:10:41,470
"Kids! Kids! Roll your way to childhood obesity!"

209
00:10:43,310 --> 00:10:45,470
Would you help me try to sell these?

210
00:10:46,220 --> 00:10:50,730
Okay. Have you considered using a girl with huge knockers?

211
00:10:51,520 --> 00:10:53,400
That's not what they're looking for.

212
00:10:53,610 --> 00:10:56,150
Hey, that would work on me.

213
00:10:56,320 --> 00:10:58,320
Why do you think I buy Mrs. Butten/vorth's?

214
00:11:07,620 --> 00:11:08,790
Hey.

215
00:11:07,620 --> 00:11:08,790
Hey.

216
00:11:08,960 --> 00:11:11,330
Hey.

217
00:11:08,960 --> 00:11:11,330
You'll never guess what just happened.

218
00:11:11,500 --> 00:11:14,170
Phoebe and I got mugged!

219
00:11:11,500 --> 00:11:14,170
Are you okay?

220
00:11:14,380 --> 00:11:16,960
Yeah, because Phoebe knew the mugger.

221
00:11:17,840 --> 00:11:19,220
How do you know a mugger?

222
00:11:19,420 --> 00:11:23,680
I'm sorry, I have friends outside the six of us.

223
00:11:23,850 --> 00:11:26,970
Know how she knew him? Because Phoebe used to mug people.

224
00:11:27,180 --> 00:11:28,890
Seriously?

225
00:11:29,060 --> 00:11:32,600
Well, I'm not proud of it, but, you know...

226
00:11:32,770 --> 00:11:37,980
when I was living on the street and I needed money for food and stuff...

227
00:11:38,190 --> 00:11:42,070
That is awful.

228
00:11:38,190 --> 00:11:42,070
I wasn't rich like you guys, okay?

229
00:11:42,240 --> 00:11:45,780
I didn't eat gold and have a flying pony.

230
00:11:46,490 --> 00:11:50,660
I had a hard life. My mother was killed by a drug dealer.

231
00:11:50,870 --> 00:11:54,000
Your mother killed herself.

232
00:11:50,870 --> 00:11:54,000
She was a drug dealer.

233
00:11:56,460 --> 00:12:01,430
It was a good thing Phoebe knew him. I was about to do some serious damage.

234
00:12:01,630 --> 00:12:03,010
Okay.

235
00:12:04,680 --> 00:12:07,680
This must have brought back some bad memories for you, Ross.

236
00:12:07,890 --> 00:12:10,680
Why?

237
00:12:07,890 --> 00:12:10,680
Well, Ross was mugged as a kid.

238
00:12:10,890 --> 00:12:14,150
You were?

239
00:12:10,890 --> 00:12:14,150
Yeah. And it was pretty traumatic.

240
00:12:14,310 --> 00:12:16,480
It was outside St. Mark's Comics.

241
00:12:16,650 --> 00:12:21,650
I was minding my business, seeing what kind of trouble Spider-Man got into.

242
00:12:21,860 --> 00:12:23,910
Ahem, Wonder Woman. Ahem.

243
00:12:25,070 --> 00:12:27,200
Anyway, I was heading towards this bakery...

244
00:12:27,370 --> 00:12:30,830
to pick up a couple of dozen linzer tortes for someone...

245
00:12:33,830 --> 00:12:37,290
when out of nowhere, this thug with a pipe jumps out and says:

246
00:12:37,460 --> 00:12:39,760
nan

247
00:12:37,460 --> 00:12:39,760
Oh, my God.

248
00:12:39,920 --> 00:12:42,800
I know. And the worst part was they took my backpack...

249
00:12:42,970 --> 00:12:48,810
which had all the original artwork I had done for my own comic book, Science Boy.

250
00:12:49,310 --> 00:12:52,180
Oh, yeah! What was his superpower again?

251
00:12:52,390 --> 00:12:55,270
A superhuman thirst for knowledge.

252
00:12:57,520 --> 00:12:59,060
I better get to class.

253
00:12:59,190 --> 00:13:02,400
Are there any more of your friends I should look out for on my way?

254
00:13:02,610 --> 00:13:05,700
No. Actually, you might wanna stay away from Jane Street.

255
00:13:05,860 --> 00:13:07,410
That's where Stabby Joe works.

256
00:13:12,540 --> 00:13:15,370
Okay, I think we have a problem here.

257
00:13:12,540 --> 00:13:15,370
What?

258
00:13:15,580 --> 00:13:20,710
Well, um, back in my mugging days, I, um, worked St. Mark's Comics.

259
00:13:20,880 --> 00:13:23,800
Yeah?

260
00:13:20,880 --> 00:13:23,800
Well, a pipe was my weapon of choice...

261
00:13:25,630 --> 00:13:28,800
and, um, preteen comic-book nerds were my meat.

262
00:13:30,560 --> 00:13:31,600
So?

263
00:13:31,810 --> 00:13:35,270
There was one kid who had a sticker on his backpack that said:

264
00:13:35,480 --> 00:13:37,690
"Geology rocks!"

265
00:13:40,820 --> 00:13:44,740
Oh, my God!

266
00:13:40,820 --> 00:13:44,740
I know! I mugged Ross!

267
00:13:51,660 --> 00:13:53,580
You're late.

268
00:13:51,660 --> 00:13:53,580
I know. I'm sorry.

269
00:13:53,750 --> 00:13:55,500
But can I just run to the bathroom?

270
00:13:55,710 --> 00:13:59,710
No. Leonard doesn't wait.

271
00:13:55,710 --> 00:13:59,710
But I am bursting with Yoo-hoo!

272
00:14:01,000 --> 00:14:03,590
Joey, here we go! Let's go. Very quickly.

273
00:14:03,800 --> 00:14:06,170
I really need...

274
00:14:03,800 --> 00:14:06,170
We must go now, quickly.

275
00:14:06,380 --> 00:14:09,430
Yeah. Yes, sir. Ahh.

276
00:14:06,380 --> 00:14:09,430
Ready?

277
00:14:10,300 --> 00:14:14,180
What the hell are you still doing here?

278
00:14:10,300 --> 00:14:14,180
I think you know!

279
00:14:15,060 --> 00:14:18,940
Oh, you sick bastard!

280
00:14:15,060 --> 00:14:18,940
I am what you made me! Know what?

281
00:14:19,100 --> 00:14:21,860
What?

282
00:14:19,100 --> 00:14:21,860
I could go right now.

283
00:14:24,070 --> 00:14:29,910
Then go. Go!

284
00:14:24,070 --> 00:14:29,910
Oh, I can't. I want to, but I can't!

285
00:14:32,580 --> 00:14:35,290
Cut. That was good!

286
00:14:35,450 --> 00:14:39,000
Very good. You did everything I asked.

287
00:14:35,450 --> 00:14:39,000
I did?

288
00:14:39,170 --> 00:14:42,750
Yes. Plus which, you've got this, I don't know, this squirmy quality...

289
00:14:43,250 --> 00:14:45,920
you bring to the character I couldn't have imagined.

290
00:14:46,130 --> 00:14:47,630
Wow, hey, here's what we're gonna do:

291
00:14:47,800 --> 00:14:50,340
Come back tomorrow for the final callbacks.

292
00:14:50,510 --> 00:14:53,640
Do all of this, what you got going now. But you know what?

293
00:14:53,810 --> 00:14:55,390
More. More. Can you do that?

294
00:14:55,560 --> 00:14:59,900
Sure. I don't have time to say thank you because I really gotta go!

295
00:15:01,350 --> 00:15:05,320
Look at that! Still in character. I like him.

296
00:15:05,480 --> 00:15:10,280
I plant seeds. I can't explain it. I don't know.

297
00:15:14,490 --> 00:15:17,250
Hey. What are you doing?

298
00:15:14,490 --> 00:15:17,250
Hey. Putting on the sneakers...

299
00:15:17,410 --> 00:15:20,210
to get in the young mindset, see if it sparks anything.

300
00:15:20,370 --> 00:15:23,080
Oh, anything yet?

301
00:15:20,370 --> 00:15:23,080
Yes, how's this?

302
00:15:23,250 --> 00:15:28,260
"They're so uncomfortable, it's like getting kicked in the nuts for your feet."

303
00:15:31,300 --> 00:15:33,470
Hey.

304
00:15:31,300 --> 00:15:33,470
Hey.

305
00:15:41,940 --> 00:15:44,520
You're probably wondering what I'm doing. Ha, ha.

306
00:15:44,810 --> 00:15:46,320
No, that seems about right.

307
00:15:47,320 --> 00:15:52,160
Yesterday at my audition, I had to pee. Apparently, that makes me a good actor.

308
00:15:52,320 --> 00:15:54,910
I got a callback, so I'm drinking everything. Oh, by the way...

309
00:15:55,080 --> 00:15:57,830
Mm-hm.

310
00:15:55,080 --> 00:15:57,830
that eggnog in our fridge was great!

311
00:15:57,990 --> 00:16:02,580
Joey, that was formula.

312
00:15:57,990 --> 00:16:02,580
We gotta get more of that.

313
00:16:04,540 --> 00:16:08,880
These aren't half bad. You should suggest these to Ralph Lauren.

314
00:16:09,090 --> 00:16:14,220
Okay, first of all, that's stupid. Second, I'm not allowed to talk to Ralph.

315
00:16:14,640 --> 00:16:18,720
All right. I feel younger already.

316
00:16:21,390 --> 00:16:23,940
Yeah, I think I broke my hip.

317
00:16:26,270 --> 00:16:27,770
PHOEBE: Hey, you!

318
00:16:26,270 --> 00:16:27,770
Hey.

319
00:16:27,980 --> 00:16:30,530
Hey. How was class?

320
00:16:31,320 --> 00:16:33,450
No one ever asks me that. What's wrong?

321
00:16:34,610 --> 00:16:37,660
Nothing. I really wanna know.

322
00:16:34,610 --> 00:16:37,660
Oh, uh.

323
00:16:37,830 --> 00:16:42,210
Well, there was actually a rather lively discussion about the Pleistocene...

324
00:16:42,370 --> 00:16:44,920
All right, nothing is worth this.

325
00:16:46,170 --> 00:16:48,830
Um, I have a confession to make. Um...

326
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:52,010
Okay, you know that, um, girl that mugged you when you were a kid?

327
00:16:52,550 --> 00:16:57,890
What are you talking about? It wasn't a girl. It was this huge dude.

328
00:16:58,100 --> 00:17:01,600
You don't have to lie anymore. I know that it was a 14-year-old girl.

329
00:17:01,810 --> 00:17:03,350
No, it wasn't.

330
00:17:01,810 --> 00:17:03,350
Yes, it was.

331
00:17:03,560 --> 00:17:07,730
No, it wasn't. You don't think I would have defended myself against a 14-year-old...?

332
00:17:07,940 --> 00:17:11,650
"Give me your money, punk!"

333
00:17:07,940 --> 00:17:11,650
Oh, my God, it was you!

334
00:17:13,190 --> 00:17:17,120
I can't believe it. You mugged me?

335
00:17:17,870 --> 00:17:21,370
Yeah. And I'm so, so sorry, Ross. I'm sorry.

336
00:17:21,540 --> 00:17:24,250
But, you know, if you think about it, it's kind of neat.

337
00:17:26,000 --> 00:17:30,130
I mean, well, it's just that I've always felt kind of like an outsider.

338
00:17:30,300 --> 00:17:33,840
You know, the rest of you have these connections that go way back...

339
00:17:34,010 --> 00:17:38,640
and, you know, now you and I have a great one.

340
00:17:39,760 --> 00:17:41,600
It's not the best!

341
00:17:42,600 --> 00:17:45,890
I know. Please forgive me. I don't know what to say.

342
00:17:46,100 --> 00:17:49,810
There's nothing you can say! That was the most humiliating thing ever.

343
00:17:50,020 --> 00:17:53,230
Really? Even more humiliating than...

344
00:17:50,020 --> 00:17:53,230
Let's not do this!

345
00:17:56,320 --> 00:18:00,080
And then, at the end of the commercial, the girls get out of the hot tub...

346
00:18:00,240 --> 00:18:02,700
and start making out with each other. Huh? Huh? Huh?

347
00:18:04,830 --> 00:18:07,290
That's interesting.

348
00:18:07,830 --> 00:18:11,340
Just one thought: You didn't mention the shoes.

349
00:18:13,670 --> 00:18:16,470
Who's next? Chandler.

350
00:18:13,670 --> 00:18:16,470
Okay.

351
00:18:16,970 --> 00:18:19,470
You start on the image of a guy putting on the shoes.

352
00:18:19,640 --> 00:18:21,680
He's about my age.

353
00:18:19,640 --> 00:18:21,680
Pfft! Your age?

354
00:18:21,850 --> 00:18:23,560
Uh-huh.

355
00:18:24,220 --> 00:18:27,270
So he's rolling down the street and he starts to lose control.

356
00:18:27,440 --> 00:18:29,980
Maybe he falls. Maybe he hurts himself.

357
00:18:30,150 --> 00:18:33,860
Just then, a kid comes flying by wearing the shoes.

358
00:18:34,030 --> 00:18:37,650
He jumps over the old guy and laughs. And the line reads:

359
00:18:37,820 --> 00:18:40,530
"Not suitable for adults."

360
00:18:41,410 --> 00:18:45,370
Well, Chandler, that's great.

361
00:18:41,410 --> 00:18:45,370
Oh, thank you, sir.

362
00:18:45,540 --> 00:18:48,540
Or, man who's two years younger than me.

363
00:18:49,830 --> 00:18:54,630
You see, that has a clear selling point. It appeals to our key demographic.

364
00:18:54,800 --> 00:18:57,800
How did you come up with that?

365
00:18:54,800 --> 00:18:57,800
I don't know! I don't know!

366
00:18:57,970 --> 00:19:03,680
I was just trying to get into a young mindset, and stuff started to flow.

367
00:19:05,600 --> 00:19:08,520
That is great. Good work.

368
00:19:05,600 --> 00:19:08,520
Thank you.

369
00:19:08,730 --> 00:19:10,690
We'll see all of you tomorrow.

370
00:19:20,740 --> 00:19:23,620
The cold weather hurts my hip.

371
00:19:28,290 --> 00:19:34,750
Hey, Ross. I know you're still mad at me, but can I just talk to you for a sec?

372
00:19:34,960 --> 00:19:38,460
Sure, go ahead. Oh, sorry. Sure, go ahead.

373
00:19:39,800 --> 00:19:42,930
I just really wanted to apologize again.

374
00:19:43,090 --> 00:19:47,930
And also show you something I think you'll find very exciting.

375
00:19:49,640 --> 00:19:52,270
Oh, my God! "Crap from the street!"

376
00:19:57,730 --> 00:20:00,320
Look, Ross. In this box...

377
00:20:00,490 --> 00:20:05,070
are all the things I got from mugging that I thought were too special to sell...

378
00:20:05,240 --> 00:20:06,280
or smoke.

379
00:20:08,750 --> 00:20:11,750
Anyway, I was looking through it, and I found...

380
00:20:12,420 --> 00:20:14,210
Science Boy.

381
00:20:15,670 --> 00:20:18,760
Qh, my God!

382
00:20:20,670 --> 00:20:23,130
I never thought I'd see this again.

383
00:20:20,670 --> 00:20:23,130
Yeah.

384
00:20:23,300 --> 00:20:24,340
What...?

385
00:20:25,680 --> 00:20:27,060
It's all here!

386
00:20:27,220 --> 00:20:28,510
Yeah.

387
00:20:27,220 --> 00:20:28,510
Ha, ha.

388
00:20:28,970 --> 00:20:31,770
What made you save it all these years?

389
00:20:31,980 --> 00:20:34,440
I guess I just thought it was really good.

390
00:20:34,600 --> 00:20:36,980
And maybe it would be worth something one day.

391
00:20:37,820 --> 00:20:41,320
You really thought Science Boy was worth saving?

392
00:20:41,530 --> 00:20:46,620
Yeah. But you should know I also have a jar of Vaseline and a cat skull in here.

393
00:20:49,330 --> 00:20:52,330
Still, this is amazing!

394
00:20:52,500 --> 00:20:54,460
Oh, my God. Thank you, Phoebe.

395
00:20:54,670 --> 00:20:59,090
You're welcome. And thank you for Science Boy. I learned a lot from him.

396
00:20:59,670 --> 00:21:01,170
You're welcome.

397
00:21:04,010 --> 00:21:07,550
I need an answer!

398
00:21:04,010 --> 00:21:07,550
I can't tell you something I don't know.

399
00:21:07,720 --> 00:21:09,640
You know!

400
00:21:07,720 --> 00:21:09,640
I don't know!

401
00:21:09,850 --> 00:21:15,770
I need an answer now!

402
00:21:09,850 --> 00:21:15,770
You want an answer? The answer is...

403
00:21:20,320 --> 00:21:22,240
Aw...

404
00:21:23,530 --> 00:21:26,070
She never loved me. She only loved you.

405
00:21:26,280 --> 00:21:28,990
You knew this all along and you never told me?

406
00:21:29,160 --> 00:21:34,250
I can never forgive you, or myself. I have nothing to live for. Bang! And scene!

407
00:21:36,250 --> 00:21:38,500
Absolutely amazing.

408
00:21:40,750 --> 00:21:44,800
The part is yours.

409
00:21:40,750 --> 00:21:44,800
Thanks! Now I really got to get going.

410
00:21:45,010 --> 00:21:48,930
Wait, wait, wait! Congratulations. You did it.

411
00:21:49,100 --> 00:21:52,930
You did it. You can relax now. Yeah.

412
00:22:05,610 --> 00:22:07,820
Wow! That's a big cable bill.

413
00:22:09,780 --> 00:22:13,120
Ha. You don't have a job, but you have no problem ordering porn.

414
00:22:14,580 --> 00:22:17,080
On a Saturday afternoon?

415
00:22:17,420 --> 00:22:19,790
I was in the house!

416
00:22:22,000 --> 00:22:25,300
Hey, uh, Phoebe didn't by any chance mention that...

417
00:22:25,510 --> 00:22:27,970
She was the huge guy that mugged you? Yeah.

418
00:22:29,090 --> 00:22:31,680
I see. You didn't happen to tell...

419
00:22:31,890 --> 00:22:35,520
Everybody we know? Yeah.

420
00:22:31,890 --> 00:22:35,520
Great. Thanks.

